    "evidence_text": "Michigan's 13th congressional district\n\nMichigan's 13th congressional district is a United States congressional district in Wayne County, Michigan.\n\nCarolyn Cheeks Kilpatrick\n\n In August 2010 she lost the Democratic primary election.\n\n She was replaced by Hansen Clarke in January 2011.\n\nElectoral history of Hansen Clarke\n\nHansen Clarke is a politician from the state of Michigan.\n\n In 2005, Clarke unsuccessfully ran for Mayor of Detroit.\n\nGary Peters (politician)\n\n The district includes the eastern half of Detroit, as well as the Grosse Pointes, Hamtramck, Southfield and Pontiac.\n\n He previously represented Michigan 's 9 congressional district from 2009 to 2013.\n\nRick Nolan\n\nHansen Clarke\n\nHansen Clarke (born March 2, 1957) is an American politician and former U.S. Congressman and Representative-elect in the 14th Congressional District of Michigan.\n\n Clarke was also the first U.S. Congressman of Bangladeshi descent.\n\nBill Foster (politician)\n\n He is a member of the Democratic Party.\n\nAdam Kinzinger\n\n He is a member of the Republican Party.\n\nBarbara Lee",
